* Transformation to a new unit cell (NEWCELL)

+ List of longest-reach cells with increasing size
# n = size of the supercell is n times the input cell.
# reach = half the length of the shortest lattice vector of the supercell (bohr).
# reach0 = reach of the longest-reach cell of that size, for comparison
# nops = symmetry operations of the crystal compatible with the supercell lattice;
# nindep, ndisp = independent atoms and displacements
# For each size, the LONGEST-REACH cell among those with the FEWEST DISPLACEMENTS
# of that size.
# newcell transformation = use these parameters in a NEWCELL command to obtain the
# Delaunay-reduced cell of this sublattice
#n   reach   reach0  nops nindep ndisp  -- NEWCELL transformation --
